Given curve, \( y=\cos x \) between \( x=0 \) and \( x=\pi \)<br>So, required area is given by<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\int_{0}^{\pi}|\cos x| d x=\int_{0}^{\pi / 2}(\cos x) d x+\int_{\pi / 2}^{\pi}(-\cos x) d x \\
\int_{0}^{\pi}|\cos x| d x=\left.(\sin x)\right|_{0} ^{\pi / 2}+.\left.(-\sin x)\right|_{\Pi / 2} ^{\Pi} \\
=1+1=\text { 2sq.units. }
\end{array}
\]

Given lines, \( y=x, y=0, x=-1 \) and \( x=2 \)<br><img src="/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkcet%252Fsol_426.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2" data-qx-orig-src="https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkcet%2Fsol_426.png?alt=media" data-qx-storage-src="https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkcet%2Fsol_426.png?alt=media"><br>So, required area is given by<br>The area of shaded region<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
=\frac{1}{2} \times|x|+\frac{1}{2} \times 2 \times 2 \\
=\frac{1}{2}+2=\frac{5}{2} \text { sq. units }
