\]

Given that, probability of defective pens is<br>\[
P=\frac{10}{100}=\frac{1}{10}
\]<br>So, probability of non-defective pens is<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
Q=1-P=\frac{9}{10} \\
\text { Since, } n=5, x \leq 1 \text {. So, } \\
P(x \leq 1)=P(x=0)+P(x=1) \\
=\binom{5}{0}\left(\frac{1}{10}\right)^{0}\left(\frac{9}{10}\right)^{5}+\binom{5}{1}\left(\frac{1}{10}\right)^{1}\left(\frac{9}{10}\right)^{4} \\
=\left(\frac{9}{10}\right)^{5}+\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{9}{10}\right)^{4}
\end{array}
\]

